        "q1": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What\u2019s the difference between fly tying materials and supplies?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Materials go on the hook. Feathers, beads, shanks, dubbing, flash. Tools and adhesives are supplies. Different aisle.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What should I buy for freshwater vs saltwater or steelhead?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Trout: softer fiber, dubbing, lighter beads. Steelhead and salt: stronger wire, flash, articulated shanks.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Where should a beginner start?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Grab a vise, then one category from the rail. Feathers or beads. Expand after you know what you burn through.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Where do you ship from?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>From the Ilwaco, Washington shop. Nationwide.</p>"
